diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 1bb9dbd..2e1c094 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
   * The Excel report adds KEV, KEV Due Date, Known Ransomware Use, Highest EPSS, and EPSS Percentile columns
   * Library finding pages show a KEV badge and EPSS score for each CVE ID, and the findings library and report findings tables show one KEV badge and the highest EPSS score per finding
   * A new EPSS threshold setting (10% by default) highlights high scores and sets `totals.findings_epss_over`
+  * Every KEV and EPSS date also comes in `YYYY-MM-DD` form, in a key ending in `_iso` (such as `finding.kev_due_date_iso`), so templates can compare dates whatever the server's date format
 
 ### Fixed
 
diff --git a/DOCS/features/findings-library/populating-the-findings-library.mdx b/DOCS/features/findings-library/populating-the-findings-library.mdx
index 3335e38..773a8a2 100644
--- a/DOCS/features/findings-library/populating-the-findings-library.mdx
+++ b/DOCS/features/findings-library/populating-the-findings-library.mdx
@@ -47,3 +47,7 @@ docker compose -f production.yml run --rm django python manage.py extract_cves
 ```
 
 By default, the command updates the findings library and findings attached to reports. Add `--library-only` or `--reports-only` to limit it to one of them, and `--verbosity 2` to list each finding it changes. Upgrades never run the command for you.
+
+<Warning>
+The command adds every CVE ID a finding's text mentions, including CVE IDs cited only as examples. A finding about vulnerable VPN appliances may name a dozen well-known CVEs that a given client doesn't have, and once they are in **CVE IDs**, reports show their KEV status and EPSS scores as if they were present. Run with `--dry-run --verbosity 2` first, and skip libraries whose findings cite example CVEs, such as Sibylline's class findings, which set **CVE IDs** themselves.
+</Warning>
